(686,	'Heliotropex N (IFF)',	NULL,	'AC',	'',	5,	NULL,	'N/a mixture',	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	'',	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	0,	'For example in floral scents such as heliotrope, acacia, lilac and honeysuckle. In addition, in gourmand scents and ambers. In most fragrance applications it can replace heliotropine/piperonal one on one. The advantage over heliotropine is that it discolours much less easily',	'Heart',	NULL,	'Me lembra cheiro de remédio, meio que cheiro de poto. mysterious exotic floral characteristic, sweet, balsamic, spicy undertones, and has nuances of almond and berries. Heliotropex N (IFF) has a deep and mysterious exotic floral characteristic, with sweet, balsamic and spicy undertones, and has nuances of almond and berries. Heliotropex N (IFF) is an economical substitute for Heliotropine when used at 15%.',	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	100,	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	NULL,	0,	0,	0,	'',	1,	NULL,	'2024-04-24 15:18:41'),
